    "title": "El Paso's 5th Annual Mija Market Returns Bigger Than Ever - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Iris Lopez ,\n9 hours ago\nEl Paso, get ready to shop, eat, and celebrate Hispanic Heritage Month in the most Borderland way possible. The 5th Annual Mija Market is going BIGGER than ever with over 80 local businesses and food vendors taking over the Cowtown Event Center on Saturday, September 27. And yes, admission is totally FREE.\nThis isn’t just a market! It’s a full-on movement. Started five years ago by nonprofit Mija, Yes You Can , the Mija Market has grown into the ultimate space for locals to support small businesses, discover creatives, and give back to the community.\nCourtesy: Iris Lopez Have Fun While Supporting TWO Local Causes: Every purchase helps fund Mija’s mentorship, scholarships, and empowerment programs for young women across El Paso. Earlier this month the organization awarded $12,000 in scholarships to local women, bringing their total to over $70K!\nGuests can expect cultural pride on full display with live performances from DJ Rach Oh, Sun City Musical Arts Drumline, Mariachi Los Pasajeros, and headliner Jezzika Sax. Plus, limited-edition tees will be sold to raise funds for Sun City Musical Arts , giving high school students access to music education and opportunities.\nCourtesy: Iris Lopez Download the KSII Mobile App Now El Paso: Make The Mija Market A Family Event Bring your friends, bring your family, and most importantly bring your appetite. Between shopping, raffles, and entertainment, the Mija Market is the can’t-miss event of the season.\nGuests are also encouraged to bring their own lawn chairs if they want to enjoy the live music. There will be open space available for guests to dance or watch the show front and center!\nCourtesy: Iris Lopez 5th Annual Mija Market:\nCowtown Event Center: 11451 Gateway Blvd W. Saturday, Sept. 27 | 10 AM – 3:30 PM FREE + Family-Friendly Mija Market Music Lineup:\nDJ Rach Oh → 10AM – 11AM Sun City Musical Arts Drum Line → 11AM – 12PM Mariachi Los Pasajeros → 12:30PM – 1:30PM MAIN ACT: Jezzika Sax → 2:30PM – 3:30PM\n2025 Mija, Yes You Can Scholarship Winners Six El Paso women were awarded a $2,000 scholarship thanks to the local organization, ‘Mija, Yes You Can.' Gallery Credit: Mija, Yes You Can Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Courtesy: Iris Lopez 2025 Mija Scholarship Awards Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market Mija Market Mija Market 2023 Mija Market Mija Market",
